+# Morning Report — ACP Subagent Grouping & Virtual Transcripts
+
+**Branch:** `feature/acp-subagent-grouping` (off `zedium-applied`, in the `zed/` submodule)
+**Date:** 2026-06-23 → overnight
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-23-acp-subagent-grouping-design.md`
+
+## TL;DR
+
+Built the feature end-to-end: external ACP providers that express subagents as flat
+same-session tool calls (qwen-code, verified live on the wire) now get their subagent
+steps **grouped out of the main transcript** into an expandable card, with a **pop-out
+focused view** of just that subagent's transcript. The model/logic layer is unit-tested;
+the UI layer is compile-verified and logic-reviewed but **not yet runtime/visually verified
+in the live app** (see Blocked/Parked).
+
+## Shipped (verified)
+
+| Milestone | Commit | What | Verification |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| M1–M3 model+adapters+ingest | `2ba2c25d52` | `SubagentGrouping` trait, `Qwen`/`Native` adapters, `SubagentIndex` on `AcpThread`, ingest classification in upsert/update | `cargo test -p acp_thread` → 76 passed (6 new) |
+| M4 adapter selection | `1d9733472c` | `AcpConnection` picks `QwenSubagentGrouping` by agent name; exposes `subagent_grouping()` | `cargo check -p agent_servers` exit 0 |
+| M5 group rendering | `bd007a680e` | Hide same-thread members from flat list; render roots as expandable subagent group | `cargo test -p acp_thread` 76; `cargo check -p agent_ui` clean |
+| M6 pop-out focused view | (pending this run's verify) | Per-subagent focused transcript + breadcrumb back; "Open" button on the group | `cargo check -p agent_ui` (in progress) |
+
+**How subagents cross the wire (verified live with `qwen --acp` v0.19.1):** single session;
+the subagent invocation is a tool call with `_meta.toolName=="agent"`; each child step is a
+flat top-level tool call tagged `_meta.{provenance:"subagent", parentToolCallId, subagentType}`.
+Captured in `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-23-qwen-acp-wire-capture.log` and distilled to the
+test fixture `crates/acp_thread/src/tests/qwen_subagent_session_updates.jsonl`.
+
+## Decisions needing your review (highest stakes)
+
+1. **Native subagent path left untouched (scoping).** This iteration generalizes only the
+   SAME-SESSION shape (qwen). Zed-native subagents (separate child session +
+   `subagent_session_info`) keep their existing card/fullscreen path. The `NativeSubagentGrouping`
+   adapter is implemented + unit-tested (proving the trait is provider-general) but
+   `NativeAgentConnection` is NOT wired to return it, and the new group/pop-out path is gated
+   on `SubagentIndex::is_same_thread_root` so native cannot be double-rendered. **Seam to flip
+   later:** wire `NativeAgentConnection::subagent_grouping()` + let the new card path handle
+   `ExternalSession` roots, then retire the legacy native card. Rationale: avoid regressing a
+   working feature and avoid recompiling the large `agent` crate overnight.
+
+2. **Provider detection by name string `"qwen-code"`** (`agent_servers/src/acp.rs`,
+   `subagent_grouping` selection). If qwen changes its reported `agentInfo.name` this silently
+   reverts to flat rendering. It's a one-line, well-marked match. Consider a capability/meta
+   sniff instead if you want robustness.
+
+3. **Pop-out is a visibility filter over the same `ListState`, not a separate view.** Focused
+   mode renders only the subtree's entries and zero-height `Empty` for the rest (no list-state
+   surgery — lowest risk). Trade-off: scroll metrics include the hidden (zero-height) slots;
+   should be visually fine but is the kind of thing to eyeball.
+
+## Decisions made (FYI, reversible)
+
+- Membership stored in a side-index keyed by `ToolCallId` rather than widening `ToolCall`.
+- Classification runs on the raw `acp::ToolCall`/`acp::ToolCallUpdate` at ingest (the converted
+  Zed `ToolCall` drops arbitrary `_meta`).
+- Lazy parent-pointer resolution with a depth-64 cycle guard (tolerates out-of-order arrival).
+- Group card reuses `render_tool_call` for the summary body and `render_entry` for member rows
+  rather than re-implementing the elaborate native card.
+
+## Blocked / parked
+
+- **Runtime/visual verification not done.** `cargo check`/unit tests pass, but I did not launch
+  the Zed app against `qwen --acp` to see the card/pop-out render. The model-layer logic (which
+  decides grouping) is unit-tested; the rendering is review-verified only. **To finish to 100%:**
+  run Zed, open the agent panel with the qwen ACP agent, issue a subagent-forcing prompt, and
+  confirm (a) members are absent from the flat transcript, (b) the group card + step disclosure
+  appear, (c) "Open" pops out the focused subagent transcript and "Back" returns, (d) native
+  subagents still render as before.
+- **Recursive deep nesting unverified.** The live capture is depth-1 only. The data model
+  supports arbitrary depth (parent pointers), but the Qwen adapter classifies a node as root
+  XOR member, so a nested "agent" call that is *also* a subagent child isn't fully linked. If
+  qwen nests in practice, the adapter needs to emit Root-with-parent. Deferred; flagged.
+- **No agent_ui render test added.** The agent_ui test harness for a full `ThreadView` is heavy;
+  I relied on the thoroughly-tested model layer instead. A focused render test would raise
+  confidence on the skip/visibility logic.
+
+## State of the tree
+
+- Branch `feature/acp-subagent-grouping`, 4 feature commits on top of the spec commit.
+- `acp_thread`: green (76 tests). `agent_servers`: green (check). `agent_ui`: M5 green; M6 verify
+  in progress at time of writing — see PLAN.md/WORKLOG.md for the final status line.
+- Local only. Nothing pushed. No PR.
+
+## Recommended next steps
+
+1. Visually verify with live qwen (the manual steps above). This is the one gap to "done".
+2. Decide on the native unification (Decision 1) — flip the seam or keep the split intentionally.
+3. If qwen nesting matters, extend `QwenSubagentGrouping` to Root-with-parent + recursive group
+   rendering (the renderer already calls `render_entry`, which would recurse into nested groups).
+4. Consider an agent_ui render test for the visibility/skip logic.
