+## 2026-06-23 23:55 MSK — M4 GREEN (commit 1d9733472c). Planning M5/M6.
+- M4: AcpConnection selects QwenSubagentGrouping when telemetry_id=="qwen-code";
+  exposes via subagent_grouping(). NativeAgentConnection deliberately NOT wired this
+  iteration (avoids recompiling the big `agent` crate + keeps native on its proven path).
+- M5/M6 design decisions:
+  * Member-skip done at the LIST PROCESSOR level (render_entries), returning Empty for
+    SameThread members — keeps render_entry pure so the group card can re-render members.
+  * SameThread roots intercepted in render_any_tool_call BEFORE the existing is_subagent()
+    branch; rendered by a new render_subagent_group that reuses render_tool_call for the
+    summary body + render_entry for expandable member rows. Toggle via expanded_tool_calls.
+  * Native (ExternalSession) roots stay on the existing render_subagent_card path. The new
+    path is gated on subtree==SameThread (new index helper is_same_thread_root) — defense
+    in depth so native cannot be double-rendered.
+  * M6 pop-out (if budget allows): a focused-visibility predicate over the SAME list_state
+    (zero-height Empty for non-subtree indices) + breadcrumb back. No list_state surgery.
+- UNCERTAINTY (flagged): live qwen capture is depth-1 only. Recursive nesting is supported
+  in the DATA model (parent pointers) but unverified against real data, and the Qwen
+  adapter currently classifies a node as root XOR member (a nested agent call that is both
+  is not fully captured). Rendering scoped to the real depth-1 case; deep nesting deferred.
+- Decision: implement M5 myself (surgical) rather than delegate — 11k-line file, slow
+  compile cycles make subagent iteration risky.
